From ccd684c2a86eeecadd5aa100f6dbea524e9fe328 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:41:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/xenos: flat shading and base vertex

- SQ_INTERPOLATOR_CNTL's PARAM_SHADE bits were all set: every varying was
  interpolated. A set bit means interpolated, a clear one flat (found with
  piglit glsl-fs-flat-color): clear the bits of flat varyings (taken from
  the input variables: lowered IO reads every input with load_input on
  some paths, so the intrinsic says nothing about interpolation), and of
  color inputs while the rasterizer has flatshade (glShadeModel(GL_FLAT)).
- VGT_INDX_OFFSET is the base vertex of an indexed draw; it was 0.

piglit glsl-fs-flat-color, arb-provoking-vertex-render, clipflat,
line-flat-clip-color, gl-1.0-dlist-shademodel and the
arb_draw_elements_base_vertex tests pass. (A first version took every
load_input as flat and failed every dEQP case with varyings.)

